{
    "background_story": "Sugams was a young artist who found solace in the quiet rhythms of Sunday mornings. Every week, he would wake up early, before the city stirred, and take a long walk along the riverbank. The stillness of the morning, the gentle lapping of the water against the shore, and the warm sunlight peeking through the trees inspired him to create. Sugams would return home, his mind buzzing with ideas, and spend the rest of the day painting. Sundays became his sacred day, a time to recharge and express himself through art. As his reputation grew, people began to look forward to his Sunday exhibitions, where he would showcase his latest works, each one a reflection of the peace and beauty he found on those lazy Sunday mornings.",
